// F-16 wing + body lift and drag - the WHOLE jet, per 27.87 m2 reference
// area (both main wings together - each "Left wing"/"Right wing" uses it on
// its half). Illustrative, shaped after published F-16 characteristics, NOT
// official data:
// - lift slope ~0.075/deg (3D, low aspect ratio - a 2D airfoil's ~0.11 is
//   far too steep for a whole wing), small camber (CL 0.05 at 0 deg);
// - vortex lift off the strakes (LEX) keeps lift building past 15 deg to a
//   peak of ~1.77 near 30 deg (the F-16 flies to ~25 deg AoA; matches the
//   pitch model's CLmax 1.78 at Mach 0.2 - see physics::f16_pitch);
// - negative side weaker (~-1.07 max near -18 deg);
// - drag: profile + induced (k = 0.12 * CL^2 - a whole-wing table has to
//   carry it, a 2D airfoil's doesn't), turning into flat-plate drag
//   (1.25 sin^2 alpha) once stalled, out to 90 deg.
// Evenly spaced at 1 deg (not required - AirFoil::sample interpolates on
// the alpha column - just tidy). Regenerate rather than hand-edit.
// (alpha_degrees, Cl, Cd)
